Unicorn CPU emulator, popcorn fork at commit
2a9d2c61fe90215e98c6e07c5b2727076e25e913, submodule third_party/unicorn
  https://github.com/Garcia6l20/unicorn, branch popcorn
  Upstream: https://github.com/unicorn-engine/unicorn, commit
  938efd13aeab73155f31cf707a2094c6ccaa36dd, modified as follows.
  2026-09-25, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/target/arm/unicorn_arm.c: host reads and writes of the M-profile
    special registers MSP, PSP, PRIMASK, BASEPRI, BASEPRI_MAX and FAULTMASK,
    and host writes of CONTROL, work in any mode. Upstream reads them as zero
    and ignores writes when the core is in unprivileged Thread mode.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added test_arm_m_unprivileged_special_regs.
  2026-09-26, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - include/unicorn/arm.h, qemu/target/arm/unicorn_arm.c: added
    UC_ARM_REG_MSPLIM and UC_ARM_REG_PSPLIM, host access to the ARMv8-M
    stack limit registers of the current security state. Upstream has no
    register id for them.
  - bindings/: regenerated the ARM constant files of the dotnet, go, java,
    pascal, python, ruby and zig bindings with the two new register ids.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added test_arm_v8m_stack_limit_regs.
